# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the CI ASan/UBSan gate.
#
# The entries below are upstream lsquic leaks, not CWIST memory: one-time
# globals allocated inside lsquic_global_init() that lsquic_global_cleanup()
# never releases.  They surface in the HTTP/3 tests (tests/test_http3.c,
# including the connection-close coverage in Test 12) because that suite is
# what initializes and tears down lsquic in-process.
#
# Previously this file also suppressed lsquic_qdh_header_in_begin,
# lsquic_malo_create, and lsquic_bw_sampler_init.  Those turned out to be
# CWIST-reachable leaks (a header set never discarded by the H3 client, and
# lsquic_conn_get_info() allocating a sampler while the connection is being
# destroyed) and are fixed in src/net/http/http3_client.c and
# src/net/http/http3.c; the suppressions were removed so regressions there
# fail the gate again.

# Global certificate-compression cache (allocated once by
# lsquic_global_init(), never freed by lsquic_global_cleanup()).
leak:lsquic_crt_init
leak:lsquic_global_init
# Backing strings of the same cache; lsquic_str_* are its allocators.
leak:lsquic_str_new
leak:lsquic_str_append
